{#- The accessibility statement: the aim, how to report a problem, what was actually done, what is not
    claimed -- the order of the GOV.UK model statement, which puts feedback and contact directly after the
    opening statement of how accessible the site is, so a reader with a problem meets the way to report it on
    the first screen instead of 2.8 screens down (deep review 2026-09-25, FL-09). Four sections rather than
    one block of prose, because this is a page people scan for one of four things, and because the margin
    rule gives each of them a tick to aim at.

    The page carries NO address of its own. "Reporting a problem" points at the colophon at the foot of the
    page, which says the address on every page of the site, written as "name [at] host" and turned into a
    link by the script in base.html.j2. That is not squeamishness: only one element per page may carry
    id="email" (it is the hook that script uses), and site.yaml refuses a plain address anywhere in the file.

    The prose lists use the same `prose` measure as the About block, so the text column is the one the rest of
    the site sets, and the bullets hang in it rather than in the gutter, which belongs to the time axis. -#}
{% extends "base.html.j2" %}

{% block main %}

    <section id="accessibility" aria-labelledby="accessibility-h">
      <h1 id="accessibility-h" class="inset">{{ page.heading }}</h1>
{% if page.get("intro") %}
      <p class="page-intro inset">{{ m.nb(page.intro) }}</p>
{% endif %}
    </section>

    <section id="aim" aria-labelledby="aim-h">
      <h2 id="aim-h" class="inset">The aim</h2>
      <div class="prose inset">
        <p>{{ m.nb(site.accessibility.aim) }}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="report" aria-labelledby="report-h">
      <h2 id="report-h" class="inset">Reporting a problem</h2>
      <div class="prose inset">
        <p>{{ m.nb(site.accessibility.report) }}</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="done" aria-labelledby="done-h">
      <h2 id="done-h" class="inset">What was done</h2>
      <div class="prose inset">
        <p>{{ m.nb(site.accessibility.done_intro) }}</p>
        <ul class="statement" role="list">
{% for item in site.accessibility.done %}
          <li>{{ m.nb(item) }}</li>
{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="limits" aria-labelledby="limits-h">
      <h2 id="limits-h" class="inset">What is not claimed</h2>
      <div class="prose inset">
        <p>{{ m.nb(site.accessibility.limits_intro) }}</p>
        <ul class="statement" role="list">
{% for item in site.accessibility.limits %}
          <li>{{ m.nb(item) }}</li>
{% endfor %}
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

{% endblock %}
